---
import { Image, getImage } from "astro:assets";
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts.ts";
import Timeline from "../components/Timeline.jsx";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/francisroy-hero.jpeg";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Cards from "../components/Cards.astro";

// Fetch all blog posts
const rawPosts = (await getCollection("blog")).sort(
  (a, b) =>
    new Date(b.data.pubDate).getTime() - new Date(a.data.pubDate).getTime(),
); // oldest → newest

// Optimize timeline images at build time
const posts = await Promise.all(
  rawPosts.map(async (post) => {
    if (!post.data.heroImage) return post;

    const optimized = await getImage({
      src: post.data.heroImage,
      width: 600,
      height: 600,
      format: "webp",
    });

    return {
      ...post,
      data: {
        ...post.data,
        heroImage: {
          src: optimized.src,
          width: optimized.width,
          height: optimized.height,
        },
      },
    };
  }),
);
---

<BaseLayout title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1>Francis Roy Lilly</h1>
      <blockquote class="hero-quote">
        <p>It is so that the works of God might be made visible through him.</p>
        <cite>John 9:3</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        Our son Francis was born on April 1, 2025 without oxygen and suffered a
        severe brain injury. During Holy Week, we were told to say our goodbyes.
        On Easter Sunday, he began breathing on his own.
      </p>
      <a href="#story" class="cta">Read His Story</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-image">
      <Image src={heroImage} alt="Francis Roy Lilly" class="hero-img" />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="story" class="about">
    <div class="about-prose">
      <h2>Francis's Story</h2>
      <p>
        Francis Roy Lilly was born to us, John and Kara Lilly, on April 1, 2025,
        following severe complications during delivery that left him unable to
        breathe. He was without oxygen for the first 25 minutes of life and
        required extensive resuscitation. He was intubated almost immediately
        and flown to the Inova Neonatal Intensive Care Unit in Fairfax, VA.
      </p>
      <p>
        As a result of the severe brain injury he sustained during birth
        (hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy, or HIE), Francis was placed on cooling
        pads and heavily medicated due to subclinical seizures. The seizures
        could not be controlled without several different types of medication,
        and their cause could not be determined. Because of his prognosis, we
        felt very discouraged, but we continued to pray for his complete and
        total healing,
      </p>
      <p>
        On the morning of Palm Sunday, April 13, we met the godparents of
        another baby (named Thomas) born at the same hospital. We shared
        Francis's story and prognosis with them, and they told us about
        <a href="https://tvwguild.org/" target="_blank"> the story of Tom Vander Woude</a>. They
        explained how he had interceded for baby Thomas and gave us the prayer
        they had used, asking for God's help through Tom Vander Woude's
        intercession.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the Tuesday of Holy Week, we had an emotional and difficult meeting
        with our care team. The doctors told us there was nothing more they
        could do for Francis. The subclinical seizures were still present
        despite the heavy doses of medication, and an MRI brain scan revealed
        that his brain cells were dying. They suggested we prepare to say our
        goodbyes and contact our family and friends.
      </p>
      <p>
        The next night, Kara sat at the dining room table in our home and said a
        prayer:
      </p>
      <blockquote class="pull-quote">
        Thomas Vander Woude, you know the love of a parent. I beg of you to go
        before the Lord to save our son.
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        That Wednesday, the doctors began weaning Francis off the medication —
        something that every time before had sent him spiraling and worsening.
        On Holy Saturday, we planned to say our final goodbyes with our two
        girls, Bella and Maxine, along with our extended family and several
        close friends.
      </p>
      <p>
        John spent the night with Francis on Holy Thursday, and by morning he
        had started to open both eyes and had a startle reflex. On the morning
        of Good Friday, Kara visited with some family and close friends, and
        Francis started moving his eyes around the room, reacting to touch and the sound of voices, and he even managed a
        cough! To our amazement, he continued to show signs of gradual
        improvement. We asked his doctors for more time to see how he would
        progress, and they enthusiastically agreed.
      </p>
      <p>
        On Easter Sunday morning, one of the doctors called to say she thought
        Francis was ready to be extubated. She believed he could breathe on his
        own!
      </p>
      <blockquote class="pull-quote">We call it our Easter Miracle.</blockquote>
      <p>
        Francis went home not long after and continues to amaze us and exceed
        every expectation. We share updates here as he grows, heals, and recovers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cards />
  <section id="updates" class="timeline-section">
    <h2>Latest Updates</h2>
    <div class="timeline-wrapper">
      <Timeline client:only="react" posts={posts} />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  section {
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .hero {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f9f6ef 0%, #f2eede 100%);
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem;
    min-height: 100svh;
  }

  @keyframes hero-slide-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(24px);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }

  .hero-text {
    flex: 1;
    max-width: 560px;
    animation: hero-slide-in 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) 0.6s both;
  }

  .hero-text h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .hero-text p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
    margin-bottom: 1em;
  }

  .hero-quote {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--primary-color);
  }

  .hero-quote p {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.35em;
  }

  .hero-quote cite {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary-color);
  }

  .hero-image {
    flex: 1;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 460px;
    animation: hero-slide-in 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) 0.4s both;
  }

  .hero-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 16px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  }

  .cta {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--primary-color);
    color: white;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .cta:hover {
    background: var(--primary-color-hover);
    color: white;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .hero {
      flex-direction: row;
      padding: 4rem 3rem;
    }
  }

  .about {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-prose {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
    animation: hero-slide-in 0.8s linear both;
    animation-timeline: view(block 25%);
    animation-range: entry 0% cover 25%;
  }

  .about-prose h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--primary-color);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5em;
  }

  .pull-quote {
    position: relative;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 3rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--primary-color);
    border: none;
    background: none;
  }

  .pull-quote::before {
    content: "\201C";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: -0.25rem;
    font-size: 4rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--primary-color);
    opacity: 0.25;
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
  }

  .timeline-wrapper {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .timeline-section h2 {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--primary-color);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .hero-text,
    .hero-image,
    .about-prose {
      animation: none;
    }
  }
</style>
